  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186083280,
      "id": "12a5ad95-0cc9-53c5-8e1c-dae35d1c4447",
      "title": "Determining the Points Where the Normal is Horizontal or Vertical"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "cb753caa-ab49-5d3b-a920-228d6759b6c3",
      ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n$x = 2\\cos 4t + 10, y = 6\\sin 4t - 3, 0 \\le t < \\frac{π}{2}$.\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the normal to the curve is horizontal.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The normal is horizontal if the tangent is vertical. Therefore, we require ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${y}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=24\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t=0\\,⟹\\,t=0,\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & =24\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=24\\ne 0, \\\\ {y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =24\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-24\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the normal to the curve is indeed horizontal when $t=0$ and $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a37cea0d-fd90-5706-991c-44bf9cdccb9a",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "c48f50f0-5c1b-5ffe-af55-f720e27d8930",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$t = 0$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "337a8924-9478-5c93-a56c-beb819cd3792",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$t = \\frac{π}{4}$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "c9c10c8e-2e63-599c-a462-0842b89d47ca",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$t = 0$ and $t = \\frac{π}{4}$"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "7bf6a500-a1b9-51a9-84ed-c52c63ffc995",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$t = 0$ and $t = \\frac{π}{2}$"
