      "db_id": 17592186083280,
      "id": "12a5ad95-0cc9-53c5-8e1c-dae35d1c4447",
      "title": "Determining the Points Where the Normal is Horizontal or Vertical"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a484ec91-6c7f-587f-8623-84fc7e269dee",
      ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=8(t-2),\\,y=3{t}^{3}-36t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the normal to the curve is vertical.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The normal is vertical if the tangent is horizontal. Therefore, we require ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${x}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=8,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=9{t}^{2}-36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving ${y}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n9({t}^{2}-4)=0\\,⟹\\,t=\\pm 2.\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(-2) & =8\\ne 0, \\\\ {x}^{′}(2) & =8\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the normal to the curve is indeed vertical when $t=\\pm 2.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "06362da5-d6f7-516f-af44-92a598391f7d",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "dddc0cac-6ae6-5c6d-8190-f32c875f8ab9",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "t=2"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "e1550612-f9f2-5865-b318-e073aa01b6c5",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "t=\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "0b3303d8-a52d-56cf-a4e8-33edb77b0bb5",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "t=-2"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "51f3699f-5b7f-5646-9283-a93b52826511",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "t=0"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "ba89430b-6e6c-515e-895b-98e107344233",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "t=\\pm 2"
            }
          ],
